{"archetypes":[{"name":"telemetry-attribution","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Cross-cutting shell launcher pins and the new invariant scanner need specialist review for attribution regressions and false signals.","prompt_body":"Investigate the implement timing attribution changes across the launcher scripts and the new scanner in scripts/test-implement-structure.sh. Check whether every intended implement timing emitter is covered without accidentally pinning shared review surfaces, and whether the awk/grep predicates avoid false positives from comments or unrelated subcommands. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"runlog-retention","focus_area":"security","weight":1,"rationale":"Run-log artifact retention and redaction wording has subtle security and contract implications beyond generic review.","prompt_body":"Review the run-log artifact allow/deny changes, static Codex sidecar fixtures, and SECURITY.md wording about retained dynamic Codex outputs. Verify that script comments, contract docs, and tests accurately describe the actual round_artifact_included behavior and do not overstate redaction guarantees. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"ci-state-machine","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The Python CI monitor tests exercise terminal outcomes in a state machine where stubs can silently miss the intended path.","prompt_body":"Examine the added python/test_ci_monitor.py monitor-level tests against the existing RecordingRunner helpers and monitor control flow. Confirm the tests actually drive the already-merged and consecutive-status-error paths they claim to cover, with assertions that would fail for meaningful regressions rather than merely matching stub defaults. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
